   with the right name passes; last week's handoff re-dated passes. The name is authored by the same agent
   whose assurance was correctly refused, so the gate still accepts an assurance, expressed in the
   filesystem. HARDENING (all from git, no content parsing): gate on the COMMIT (committed today, by that
   resident — `git log -1 --format='%aI %an'`), assert non-trivial size (`git cat-file -s`), keep the
   filename date as an INDEX never as the EVIDENCE.

