SLASH-COMMAND SURFACE NORMALIZATION RULED (Lead's PM-requested memo; three surfaces — Slack console
  commands, web UI, CLI): ⭐ ONE REGISTRY, MANY PROJECTIONS — NOT ONE VOCABULARY.
  NORMALIZE: what commands exist, what each DOES, and whether each MUTATES (one source of truth — same
  argument as PDR-006 condition 2). DO NOT NORMALIZE: spelling and invocation form. `/standup` in Slack,
  `piper standup` in CLI, a slash-menu entry in web are THE SAME COMMAND IN THREE GRAMMARS.
  WHY FORM-PARITY IS THE ERROR: it is PA's tool-catalog finding one surface over — "the property that makes
  the alias set good input makes it bad catalog." Slack commands are FIXED/PRE-REGISTERED, web chat is
  FREE-FORM, CLI is TYPED/COMPLETABLE: three different interaction contracts.
  INVARIANT: a command with the same name means the same thing and has the same effect on every surface it
  appears on. ANTI-INVARIANT (refused): every command appears on every surface. A surface carrying a subset
  DECLARES that subset in the registry, so "absent from the CLI" is a recorded decision, not a discovered gap.
  🔴 HAZARD NO DERIVE CAN REACH: Slack's slash commands are registered BY HAND IN SLACK'S CONSOLE — outside
